  2	
  3	## Description
  4	
  5	Refactor `TestSuiteBootstrap` to replace the write-heavy `configureUsers()` with a verify-only check, add a public static `seedSystemUsers()` method with proper transaction error handling, and register a shutdown handler for transaction cleanup.
  6	
  7	## Scope
  8	
  9	- `src/classes/Application/Bootstrap/Screen/TestSuiteBootstrap.php`
 10	
 11	## Dependencies
 12	
 13	- None
 14	
 15	## Acceptance Criteria
 16	
 17	1. `configureUsers()` performs only `SELECT` queries (no `INSERT`, `UPDATE`, or transaction start/commit) — it reads system user IDs via `Application::getSystemUserIDs()` and checks existence via `AppFactory::createUsers()->idExists()`.
 18	2. When any system user ID is missing from the test database, `configureUsers()` throws a `BootException` with error code `175001` and a message containing both the missing user IDs and the text `composer seed-tests`.
 19	3. `seedSystemUsers()` is `public static`, starts a transaction, runs the `InitSystemUsers` installer task, commits on success, and rolls back via `DBHelper::rollbackConditional()` on any `\Throwable` before re-throwing.
 20	4. `registerTransactionCleanupHandler()` registers a shutdown function (via `register_shutdown_function`) that calls `DBHelper::rollbackConditional()`.
 21	5. `_boot()` calls `registerTransactionCleanupHandler()` between `configureDatabase()` and `configurePaths()`.
 22	6. The class constant `ERROR_TEST_DB_NOT_SEEDED` has an explicit `int` type declaration and value `175001`.
 23	7. All new code uses `array()` syntax (not `[]`).
 24	
